  "script": "The cutting-edge front splitter and aggressive air intake define the 2024 Corvette Z06's advanced aerodynamic capabilities. Red brake calipers complement the black rims, emphasizing the Corvette Z06's performance credentials. Quad exhaust outlets integrated into the rear diffuser enhance the Z06\u2019s performance and aerodynamic focus. The supercharger on the 5.5-liter V8 marks the Z06's commitment to power, pushing out 670 horsepower and 460 lb-ft of torque. Inside, striking red leather upholstery with contrasting stitching captures the 3LZ trim's luxurious touch. The carbon fiber rear spoiler complements the quad exhausts for a performance-oriented exterior. Paired with an 8-speed dual-clutch transmission, the Z06 delivers precise, rapid gear changes for optimal track performance. Originally priced around $110K, the Z06 now trades near $100K, holding value at roughly 2% annual depreciation. With 670 hp, it outpowers the Porsche 911 Turbo S\u2019s 640 hp. Though the Porsche hits the quarter-mile in 10.5 seconds, the Z06 isn\u2019t far at 10.6. Would you pick the Z06 for its American muscle or the 911 Turbo S for its precision engineering?",
